2018-04-03 Thore Böckelmann <tboeckel@gmx.de>

  * Window.c: added an experimental feature to support large GUIs on small
    screens. If a window does not fit on a screen MUI will now dynamically add a
    scrollable virtual group around the usual window contents instead of
    modifying the application's settings to enforce a smaller GUI due to smaller
    font and frame sizes. This will affect the sole too large window only
    instead of all windows of the application. The well known adaption of the
    settings is still used as fallback, but now is very unlikely to happen at
    all.

